From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:09:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: close a stopped stream before
 preparing it again

A STOP trigger only sends an EOS and sets the state to STOPPED: the stream stays open on the DSP until close().
q6asm_dai_prepare() cleared the previous setup only in the RUNNING state, so a prepare after a stop - PipeWire stops
and re-prepares a capture PCM without closing it - opened the stream again and the DSP refused it with ADSP_EALREADY
('DSP returned error[9]', 'q6asm_open_read failed') on every retry until the PCM was closed; seen on the Surface Duo
as a burst of a few hundred failures after a recording ended.

Clear the previous setup whenever the stream is not IDLE, and leave the state IDLE once the DSP stream is closed, so
IDLE always means 'nothing open on the DSP' (close() already relies on that).

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 854ed72c3..fe01f599d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -224,15 +224,17 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	prtd->pcm_count = snd_pcm_lib_period_bytes(substream);
-	/* rate and channels are sent to audio driver */
-	if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
-		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
+	/*
+	 * Clear the previous setup if any: the stream is open on the DSP in RUNNING and also after a STOP trigger
+	 * (STOPPED - only an EOS was sent). Re-opening it without the close fails with ADSP_EALREADY.
+	 */
+	if (prtd->state != Q6ASM_STREAM_IDLE) {
 		q6asm_cmd(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id, CMD_CLOSE);
 		q6asm_unmap_memory_regions(substream->stream,
 					   prtd->audio_client);
 		q6routing_stream_close(soc_prtd->dai_link->id,
 					 substream->stream);
-		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_STOPPED;
+		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_IDLE;
 	}
 
 	ret = q6asm_map_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client,
@@ -308,6 +310,7 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	q6asm_cmd(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,  CMD_CLOSE);
 open_err:
 	q6asm_unmap_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client);
+	prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_IDLE;
 
 	return ret;
 }
